# Golden fixtures are byte-exact reference data for the Tier 2 conformance gate.
# Never apply line-ending normalisation to them: CRLF conversion would change
# every byte and make a correct Godot port fail byte-for-byte comparison, or --
# worse -- silently change what "identical" means depending on who checked out.
fixtures/** -text

# UE-extracted scenario records are also machine-generated reference data, written by
# WorldEngine/Scripts/extract_scenario_data.py with explicit LF newlines. CRLF
# conversion would make every re-extraction show as a whole-file diff and would change
# the bytes Scenarios.cs compares against.
migration-data/*.json -text
